CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc_node(sizeof(*filters)...) over kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct etm_filters)...)
#54: FILE: drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-etm-perf.c:92:
+	filters = kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct etm_filters), GFP_KERNEL, node);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'filter->range == 1'
#116: FILE: drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-etm-perf.c:513:
+		if ((filter->range == 1) && address)

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

